Kane-Mele on the honeycomb at delta = 0 and rashba = 0, PRL 95, 226801 (2005):
one monolayer with four bands, two occupied, and an unbroken horizontal mirror,
asked three ways.
Bands are counted from 0, as pythtb counts them.

A. the layer in the plane, declared free-standing
   realized group   : #191.234 P6/mmm1', 4 bands, orbitals at Wyckoff 2c
   site irrep       : -E1, of the declared s orbital
   bands 0 and 1    : GM: -GM9   K: -K8   M: -M6
   out of the plane : 11 coreps at k_z = 1/2, measured on the layer's own stack
   indicator class  : (1, 0) in Z6 x Z12, order 6
   free-standing is a declaration: a flat model has no third coordinate, and a
   layer on a substrate has no mirror in z

B. the same layer, with the physical p_z declared
   realized group   : #191.234 P6/mmm1', orbitals at Wyckoff 2c
   site irrep       : -E2, of the declared p_z, odd under the mirror: m(z) = -1
   bands 0 and 1    : GM: -GM12   K: -K9   M: -M5
   indicator class  : (5, 0) in Z6 x Z12, order 6
   inversion        : r to -r, the product of the mirror m(z) and the rotation C2z,
                      taking site 0 to 1 and site 1 to 0
   spinor squares   : +E for the inversion, so eigenvalues +-1; Ebar for m(z) and C2z,
                      so eigenvalues +-i
   rashba = 0.25    : #183.186 P6mm1', a subgroup of index 2;
                      indicator group: trivial
   operations' R_zz : -1 and +1 at rashba = 0, only +1 at rashba = 0.25:
                      the mirror and every operation composed with it are gone
   C2z acts on in-plane k as inversion does but is a rotation: the inversion, with
   its parity eigenvalues, is the layer group's and needs the third direction

C. the layer as a periodic decoupled stack
   the stack        : 3 periodic directions and no vacuum, period c = 8
   H(k, k_z) - H(k) : 0.000000 in its largest entry, over 6 random in-plane k
                      and k_z = 0, 0.25 and 0.5
   realized group   : #191.234 P6/mmm1', orbitals at Wyckoff 2c, k-points A GM H K L M
   bands 0 and 1    : GM: -GM12   A: -A12   K: -K9   H: -H9   M: -M5   L: -L5
   indicator class  : (5, 0) in Z6 x Z12, order 6

D. the three classes side by side
   presentation     : group      indicator group   class    order   z2w,3   z4
   the plane, s     : #191.234   Z6 x Z12          (1, 0)   6       1       2
   the plane, p_z   : #191.234   Z6 x Z12          (5, 0)   6       1       2
   the stack, p_z   : #191.234   Z6 x Z12          (5, 0)   6       1       2
   named indicators : of the p_z class, z2w,3 = 1, z4 = 2, z3m,π = 2, z3m,0 = 2,
                      z6m,0 = 1, z6m,π = 1, z12 = 2
   out of the plane : z2w,3, z3m,π and z6m,π read only the coreps at k_z = 1/2,
                      z4 and z12 those of both planes
   all 4 bands      : the band representation of the orbitals at 2c, an atomic limit
   indicator class  : (0, 0) in Z6 x Z12, order 1, every named indicator 0
   the stack and the plane with p_z have one class, (5, 0); declaring s instead
   moves it to (1, 0) and leaves its order, z2w,3 and z4 as they are

E. the layer's bands, and the stack's at k_z = 0 and k_z = 1/2

